`,o.jsx(t.p,{children:"A fun little café run by friendly owners who are always happy to join you for a game. They've got a good collection, and the coffee is excellent. If you go, try a few rounds of Guess Who with friends. Btw I've never lost a single round."}),`
`,o.jsx(t.p,{children:"These spots are perfect for long, lazy game days when you don't want to host at home."}),`
`,o.jsx(t.h2,{children:"3. Nepali Board Games You Can Try and Buy"}),`
`,o.jsx(t.p,{children:"Board game Nepal is not just about imported games: local creators are making amazing ones too."}),`
`,o.jsx(t.h3,{children:"Bluff Momo – By Tumlet"}),`
`,o.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Our first game, Bluff Momo, is all about deception and Nepali humor. You'll meet characters like Hante, Aama, and Bhatti ko Dai. Bluff momo has a bit of a learning curve to it. You need to memorize different powers. But once you do that, you can end of playing for hours. I've written a detailed review of ",o.jsx(t.a,{href:"/blog/best-nepali-board-games",children:"Bluff Momo and other Nepali board games I've actually played"})," if you want to know more. It also happens to be small enough to pack in a suitcase, which is why it made our list of the ",o.jsx(t.a,{href:"/blog/best-souvenirs-nepal",children:"best souvenirs to bring home from Nepal"}),"."]}),`
